REQ-261002-FFTQ"},"type":"requirement_affected"},"detail":"Authored by our proof work (6f6a3f97, wording fixes c5313736/dd658f46), not upstream. It is `observed_pass` (3 passed) and its inherited error_handling cell is `observed_pass` (1 test). Witnesses in `menu-file-test.sh`: a link root with a loop below it lists `clip.webm` and exits 0 (line 88); a real root lists as before (line 96); a link root whose target is gone is refused through `refuse()` (line 137). On the base, find skips a link start point, so the first row would list nothing. The defensive violation row is reviewed in REVIEW-261002-6P46. Status is `review` / `in_review` (ai_generated), so it is not yet human-approved spec.","refs":[{"id":"SW-REQ-261002-FFTQ","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-file-test.sh","kind":"file","line":88},{"id":"bin/omarchy-menu-file","kind":"file","line":54}],"severity":"medium","title":"SW-REQ-261002-FFTQ (added): symbolic link roots are followed, links inside a root are not","verification":{"evidence":[{"id":"SW-REQ-261002-FFTQ","kind":"requirement"}],"method":"review.changes (spec, code-trace, function and call-level requirement impact)","note":"SW-REQ-261002-FFTQ is in review.changes (added, matchLevel function).","status":"confirmed"}},{"claim":{"params":{"requirement":"SW-REQ-261002-9H5Y"},"type":"requirement_affected"},"detail":"Authored by our proof work (6f6a3f97). It is `observed_pass` (3 passed) and its error_handling cell is `observed_pass`. Witnesses: a link root plus its target (line 105), and a root given twice, each give one `clip.webm` row; a missing path next to a real root is refused with no partial listing (line 141). REVIEW-261002-VZ1K covers the defensive row. The rationale says the key is the file, not the path, so hard links also merge, and states that the PR gives the intent for aliased roots only. Status `review` / `in_review`.","refs":[{"id":"SW-REQ-261002-9H5Y","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-file-test.sh","kind":"file"